Bug fix: Phaser ghost kills — invisible enemy no longer kills player.

This commit modifies 7 files (+289/-8 lines), spanning 2 core game loop, 2 enemy AI, 1 documentation.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
Root cause: Phaser enemy cycles through FadingIn/Visible/FadingOut/Invisible phases.
When invisible/fading, _invulnerable=true (blocks bullets) but isMaterializing=false
(collision system still ran player-enemy check). Phaser killed player while opacity=0.

Fix:
- Added isGhostForPlayer:boolean=false to BaseEnemy
- Phaser sets isGhostForPlayer=true during FadingIn/FadingOut/Invisible phases
- Phaser sets isGhostForPlayer=false during Visible phase (only time it can kill)
- CollisionSystem.checkPlayerEnemyCollisions() skips isGhostForPlayer enemies
- GameInstance._checkEnemyPlayerCollisions() same fix (test harness path)

Files: BaseEnemy.ts, Phaser.ts, CollisionSystem.ts, GameInstance.ts

Regression test: src/test/s44h-03-phaser-ghost-kills.regression.test.ts

